      "location": "Proof 1.1",
      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "The proof says, “patch them by a partition which is constant in the normal directions near each sheet, preserving the product germs,” then claims the normal exponential map identifies the collars exactly with the model sheets. The cited tubular-neighbourhood theorem supplies only a diffeomorphism from an open normal-bundle neighbourhood to an ambient neighbourhood; the product-chart lemma supplies charts near a point; and the partition-of-unity theorem supplies an ordinary subordinate partition. None establishes the required simultaneous adapted metric, special partition, or framed tube. The germ-isomorphism result only compares tubes after they exist. This is the central prerequisite for the model, not an immediate omitted coordinate detail.",
