      "id": "cor-tubular-neighbourhoods-are-unique-up-to-ambient-isotopy",
      "location": "title",
      "defect": "overstrong-title-or-statement",
      "evidence": "The title claims uniqueness for tubes on the same normal bundle. But the cited definition requires only an open normal-bundle neighbourhood and an embedding with Φ(0_p)=i(p); it does not require matching vertical derivatives. The Statement itself adds that dΦ₁ and dΦ₂ must induce the same normal-quotient map and warns that fixing the zero section alone is insufficient. For S={0}⊂R, Φ₁(v)=v and Φ₂(v)=−v are both tubes under the definition, but no isotopy of tube maps fixing S can join them: the derivative at 0 would have to vary continuously from +1 to −1 while remaining nonzero.",
