      "location": "Opening paragraph, sentence 2",
      "defect": "missing-hypothesis",
      "evidence": "The page says “tubular neighbourhoods of the same normal bundle are unique up to ambient isotopy” without the compatibility of their induced vertical normal maps. The current corollary requires those maps to agree, and the repository definition of a tubular neighbourhood requires only Φ(0_p)=i(p). The tubes v↦v and v↦−v for a point in R satisfy that definition but cannot be joined by an isotopy fixing the point, since the derivative sign cannot change through nonzero derivatives.",
